{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number attribute indicates which times the ending is played, similar to the time-only attribute used by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other elements. While this often represents the numeric values for what is under the ending line, it can also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicate whether an ending is played during a larger dal segno or da capo repeat. Single endings such as “1”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or comma-separated multiple endings such as “1,2” may be used. The ending element text is used when the text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the ending is different than what appears in the number attribute. The print-object attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used to indicate when an ending is present but not printed, as is often the case for many parts in a full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"score."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<ending>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLEnding","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV","role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/init(value:number:kind:printsObject:position:font:color:system:endLength:textX:textY:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/endLeng